e  after a workout session especially after  an intense workout you will need more  food for your body to repair and recover  so for instance if you were to burn 400  calories in a workout session it does  not necessarily mean that you have to  eat all the 400 calories back you might  find that eating an additional 200  calories is enough for you if I were to  eat back the 400 calories doesn't it  defeat the purpose of me trying to burn  the 400 calories while no exercising and  burning fat does not just stop there for  instance after an intense workout  session your body will keep burning fat  more efficiently for the next hour and  your metabolism will be increased for  the next 24 hours which means more fats  and more calories being burned so the  workout benefits continues what you  should not be practicing is the idea of  workout calories and food calories as  trade-off items for instance oh I've  been 400 calories I can have a donut now  No  not only are you really wasting your  time and effort you might be consuming  more than your workout calories in a  single donut don't work out because you  hit your body workout because you love  your body and you want to treat it right  step 5 is to keep track of yourself now  that you have your food and meal plan in  place keep track of your daily food and  physical activities self-awareness is  self motivation by keeping track of your  behavior you must avail yourself to  change by becoming more  countable keeping a food diary is the  first and most crucial step towards  weight management it is a great way to  assess your positive and negative habits  to look at areas that can be changed to  eat less to understand food calories and  to perhaps deal with emotional eating  and write everything down I mean every  single thing we tend to write our main  meals and we tend to forget about the  small nibbles you might have or even the  endless amount of coffee with milk you  might have in a day  almost everything that goes into your  mouth has calories so by writing a food  journal  you might find that it is those small  nibbles or the endless amount of coffee  with milk that is wrecking up the  additional 4 to 500 calories with this  information you can make smarter food  choices for your body and to understand  your emotion towards food so write  everything down immediately after a meal  because otherwise you will tend to  forget next step is to keep an activity  diary so write down what activity you  did how long for what was the intensity  how many calories did you burn and how  did you feel you can even be more  specific and record of the weights and  repetitions you did this is a good way  to keep track of your workouts and to  increase the weights and repetitions as  you get stronger your aim is to be able  to fill up your activity diary with 6  days of activities and one rest day in a  week so make a conscious effort to add  more activities into your days next is  to track and measure your weight loss  progress most women are obsessed over  the skill and the numbers really do  affect us basing your weight-loss  progress  solely on the skill is not accurate our  weight can fluctuate greatly from day to  day so do not measure yourself every day  in fact if you really have to only  measure yourself once a week and only  measure your weight loss progress once a  month because then you will see a much  more significant change which will keep  you  motivated do not make the skill your  only measurement of success so please do  watch my video here for other accurate  ways to measure your weight-loss success  step number six is to get support can  you lose weight on your own of course  you can but it can be challenging at  times it would be a benefit to you to  have a support network around you for  instance a workout buddy a family member  who choose for you  professionals like your personal trainer  or be part of an online community where  you can share your weight loss journey  with so for instance my youtube channel  here feel free to share your weight loss  journey ask questions and even support  each other that's what we are here for  it is very important for you to surround  yourself with positive and like-minded  people and to stay away from the  negative people who might directly or  indirectly sabotage your weight loss  goals to avoid this from happening let  us identify your indirect saboteurs  usually they will be family members or  close friends who might unintentionally  sabotage your plan for instance they  might buy you your favorite cake or  bring you to your favorite fast-food  restaurant  chances are they do not know your plan  to lose weight so speak to them and tell  them your intention to start losing  weight and to eat healthier understand  that you cannot expect them to change  their eating habits because of you but  both of you can work on a solution  together for instance if you do not have  control over your mom's cooking perhaps  you can suggest for her to cook more  vegetables to prepare a smaller portion  for you and to separate the sauce or  topping which is usually high in  calories this way you can exercise  portion control and to reduce all your  calories also like the note to stop  buying your favorite snacks and to buy  more fruits instead if you don't tell  your mom she wouldn't know if you were  to dine out with your partner or your  friend go to a place where you can make  healthier choices and both of you can  enjoy  at the same time don't be tempted to  have what they have make your own  choices know your portion and stick by  it some of you my face with direct  saboteurs people who intentionally want  to see you fail  my advice to you is to be selfish this  is your life your body and your goal if  they are not offering any support  instead they are making you feel  unworthy and to feel like a failure your  best bet is to stay away from them do  not waste your time trying to explain or  share your witness goals you do not owe  them any explanation and you should not  be guilty if you choose to avoid them  these people are usually jealous because  you're changing you're losing the weight  and you're getting in shape and they're  not so therefore to see you fail means  they can feel good about themselves and  their ego cashing out the support is  important but most importantly is self  support supporting yourself start from  your internal thoughts and emotion and  this has a huge impact on your progress  if you treat your body with love and  respect  you will naturally start feeding your  body with good food and give it the  workout it deserves  so start loving yourself by saying  positive words to yourself and reward  yourself not with food every time you  are a step closer to your goal the last  step is to take action now that you have  all the knowledge and tools you need you  are ready to go on this weight-loss  journey to a new you take one step at a  time one day at a time be consistent  with your workouts eat healthy most  times and I can assure you you will see  the result you deserve all success  stories come with willingness to change  determination taking action and to keep  trying and trying again when you fall  now that you are at the end of the video  grab a pen and paper if you  I ain't done it and start mapping out  your weight-loss journey start today not  tomorrow not next week or next month  give the gift of love back to yourself  this year all of us for new fitness food  and motivational videos please like  share and subscribe to my youtube  channel and website do follow me on  Facebook Instagram and Twitter to stay  connected with me thanks guys  you
 

